<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.17.2: What Is a Recursive Definition?</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01169</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.17.2: What Is a Recursive Definition?</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a1f6a500-f238-4200-956e-c123f469e3a4</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>The <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">recursive definition</term> is a function that provides a repeated, or recurring, process to find terms in a sequence.</para>
      <para>Start with the recursive definition: \(R(n)=3R(n-1) + 1\), \(n\geq2\) and given \(R(1)=-1\). </para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_20_03_01.png"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
      </para>
      <list>
        <item> The first part of the recursive definition provides the instructions for how to generate the sequence. It provides the function rule or formula for the nth term. </item>
        <item>The second part states the domain of the sequence. It describes where we start and the values that are substituted into the function.</item>
        <item>The third part is the basis for the sequence or the smallest term value. </item>
      </list>
      <para>See the table below for how to substitute to find more terms in the sequence using the recursive definition. Substitute the term number, \(n\), in for \(n\) in the recursive definition. Complete the table with a partner.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-wideadjustedtable">
        <thead>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>Term number (n)</emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>Substitute in \(R(n)\)</emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <emphasis>Value</emphasis>
            </entry>
          </row>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry>1</entry>
            <entry>given</entry>
            <entry>-1</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>2</entry>
            <entry>\(3R(2-1) + 1 = 3R(1) + 1 = 3(-1) + 1 = -2\)</entry>
            <entry>-2</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>3</entry>
            <entry>\(3R(3-1) + 1 = 3R(2) + 1 = 3(-2) + 1 = -5\)</entry>
            <entry>-5</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>4</entry>
            <entry>\(3R(4-1) + 1 = 3R(3) + 1 = 3(-5) + 1\)</entry>
            <entry>a. ___</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>5</entry>
            <entry>a. ___</entry>
            <entry>b. ___</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>6</entry>
            <entry>b. ___</entry>
            <entry>c. ___</entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Using the recursive definition:
        <para>Substitute \(n=5\) in \(R(n)\)</para>
        </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(3R(5-1)+1\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Substitute \(n=6\) in \(R(n)\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(3R(6-1)+1\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Determine the value for each term:<para>Value when \(n=4\)</para>
        </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>–14</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Value when \(n=5\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>–41</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Value when \(n=6\)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>–122</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Write the full sequence out to 6 terms.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>–1, –2, –5, –14, –41, –122</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <title>Activity</title>
        <exercise data-content-id="8482cb5d-ffd9-4df8-a1ea-03a368002bbc" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Determine if the following sequences are arithmetic or geometric.
          <para>3, 6, 12, 24</para>
          </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Geometric </para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is Geometric. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="e4499a8e-3c8c-4333-ac8d-a11528814f06" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>18, 36, 72, 144</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Geometric </para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is Geometric. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="510fe714-b9ad-405d-9b78-8ed6968e7062" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>3, 8, 13, 18</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Arithmetic </para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is Arithmetic. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="50feab68-5dea-4c36-be37-545bdaf60041" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>18, 13, 8, 3</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Arithmetic </para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is Arithmetic. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="cf3aaa85-e458-44cf-b486-5f63ff2a8672" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>18, 9, 4.5, 2.25</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Geometric </para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is Geometric. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="af41a1fe-53a0-42fa-a351-2dac2cdbb508" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>18, 20, 22, 24</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Arithmetic </para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is Arithmetic. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="1b175600-5dea-49f8-ac17-d905c8b82fb1" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>3, 15, 75, 375</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Geometric </para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is Geometric. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
